From: Thuong Vo <66083331+SekiroKenjii@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 07:15:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] profile: follow a rewritten user palette

A rewritten palette file replaces its PtyxisPalette in the palette list,
but a profile notifies "palette" only when its GSettings key changes, so
open terminals and the window dressing keep the old palette until
restart. Apex rewrites the user palette when the accent changes
(apex-session-agent), and the caret must follow within a second.

ptyxis_profile_constructed() calls apex_profile_follow_palette_files()
(src/apex/, Source100), which notifies "palette" when the list reloads a
palette with the profile's palette id.
---
 src/ptyxis-profile.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ptyxis-profile.c b/src/ptyxis-profile.c
index b803e8c..6d2a646 100644
--- a/src/ptyxis-profile.c
+++ b/src/ptyxis-profile.c
@@ -30,6 +30,8 @@
 #include "ptyxis-profile.h"
 #include "ptyxis-util.h"
 
+#include "apex/apex-palette.h"
+
 struct _PtyxisProfile
 {
   GObject parent_instance;
@@ -252,6 +254,8 @@ ptyxis_profile_constructed (GObject *object)
                            G_CONNECT_SWAPPED);
 
   read_custom_links_from_settings (self);
+
+  apex_profile_follow_palette_files (self);
 }
 
 static void
